                <pb facs="0620" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6292/141.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-10-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Commissioner Loomis requests the transmission of the following: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>At a sumptuous luncheon, given in honor of the American commission at the
                            Hama Palace, the minister of commerce, who is vice of the exposition,
                            officially announced that the exposition, projected on much larger
                            lines, would take place in 1917, and heartily thanked Roosevelt in the
                            Emperor’s name for his interest in the enterprise and for sending such a
                            highly competent commission to discuss the plans, scope, and details of
                            the proposed international affair.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
